{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Moses sent them.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: ״נקום נקמת״ — take vengeance yourself, yet he sends others. Rather, because he was raised in Midian, he said: it is not just that I should repay them with evil, for they did me a kindness and a benefit, as people say: into the well from which you drank water, do not throw dirt. And some say: this is not the Midian in which Moses was raised, for this is beside Moab, and to this day it is desolate. And why did he send Pinchas? One who begins a mitzvah is told to complete it — and he struck the Midianite woman, therefore let him complete his mitzvah."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:23.988376858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}